+
+// AI event pacing. By default the AI event is sent once per VI, which suits games that
+// generate one audio frame per video frame. Games that generate small fixed-size frames
+// on each AI buffer-completion event (e.g. Hey You, Pikachu!: 184 samples at 32 kHz)
+// need the event paced by audio consumption instead: with this enabled, one event is
+// sent whenever buffered audio drops below low_water_ms, and the next only after the
+// game queues its buffer. Call before the game starts.
+void set_ai_buffer_pacing(bool enabled, uint32_t low_water_ms);
+void notify_ai_buffer_queued();
 
